  "tape": "slow_orbit",
  "notes": "The slowest tape, a lullaby: felt-piano broken chords instead of Rhodes, long chords that hold for two bars, a Lydian G (maj9#11) for the floating feel, and a wide pad that drifts left and right once every four bars like something in orbit. The A theme is sung by a soft theremin-like voice that glides between notes; the B theme by a high felt piano. The only drums are a heartbeat kick, a rim on 3 and a brush stir, and only in the middle of the tape.",
